# data/ is generated by the daily Action, not written by hand. A three-way merge of a
# 100-row JSON array happily writes conflict markers *inside* the JSON, and the next run
# then dies on "Invalid numeric literal" with nothing pointing at the real cause.
#
# -merge makes git refuse to auto-merge these: it keeps our copy and reports the path as
# unresolved instead of corrupting it. Losing a side costs nothing — the next run rebuilds
# the rolling window from the API and re-merges whatever is already on the board.
#
# Diffs stay on (no -diff): the workflow writes these pretty-printed, so the daily commit
# is still readable line by line.
data/jobs.json -merge
data/meta.json -merge

# The workflow's `run:` blocks are bash. Actions normalises line endings today, but a
# CRLF shell script is a bad thing to depend on not happening.
*.yml text eol=lf
